{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>When its harvest dries up.</b> Like וטל ילין בקצירי (Job 29:19)." "<b>Are broken.</b> The branches, which are smaller than the harvest." "<b>Who kindle.</b> Some say from the root of אריתי מורי (Song of Songs 5:1), and the meaning is gatherers, and the sense is even the women who have no strength. Others say מאירות is like מבעירות, and the meaning is that they will become firewood, and this is the correct view. Like it: ולא תאירו מזבחי חנם (Malachi 1:10)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:26.737665687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}